    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 263 tests pass with 0 failures and 0 errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n**Change:** When `POST /api/owners` carries an `Idempotency-Key` header, a repeat request with an already-seen key returns the originally created owner with **200 OK** instead of creating a duplicate (which would otherwise be rejected with 409).\n\n**How it works** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- Added an in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer> idempotentCreates` mapping each seen key \u2192 the id of the owner that create produced.\n- Since the `addOwner` signature is fixed by the generated `OwnersApi` interface (no header param), I read the header via `RequestContextHolder`/`ServletRequestAttributes` in a small `currentIdempotencyKey()` helper (trims the value; treats missing/blank as \"no idempotency\").\n- At the start of `addOwner`, if the key is known, it re-fetches the original owner, rebuilds the DTO (membership + bulk-signup warning, matching `getOwner`'s response shape), and returns 200.\n- After a successful create, it records `key \u2192 owner.getId()` before returning the usual 201.\n\nA missing or blank key preserves the original behavior exactly. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreIdempotentRepeat` passes, and the full suite (263 tests) remains green.",
