    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is implemented in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(...)` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:138`), binding to the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` and persisting an `Owner`.\n\n## Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:138`). Non-admins are rejected (403).\n2. **Bean Validation on the request DTO** (`@Valid @RequestBody`, interface is `@Validated`). All in the default group (no ordering guarantee); failure \u2192 **400**:\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(1,10)` (optional)\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)` (trailing dot allowed), `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1,255)` (optional)\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1,80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)` (optional)\n   - `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid` only\n   - `sharesHousehold` \u2014 no constraint; used as a flag later, never persisted\n\n## Inside the method (this exact order)\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 reads `Idempotency-Key` header; if seen before and the original owner still exists, returns it with **200 OK** (no new create). (`:142`)\n4. **Map DTO \u2192 entity** via `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)` (ignores `id`, `pets`). (`:155`)\n5. **Address normalization** (`applyAddress`, `:156`) \u2014 prefers `addressLine1/2` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET etc.), else the flat `address`; sets those fields on the entity. Empty composed address \u2192 **400**.\n6. **Telephone \u2192 E.164** (`toE164`, `:161`) \u2014 strips separators; `+` kept, leading `0`\u2192`+61` (AU), else `+1` (NANP); must be 8\u201315 digits with valid national length. Failure \u2192 **400**. Sets normalized telephone.\n7. **Email normalization** (if present, `:167`) \u2014 regex check + reject disposable domains (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail), lower-case. Failure \u2192 **400**.\n8. **Postcode validation** (if present, `:173`) \u2014 4 digits and within the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region accepts any). Failure \u2192 **400**.\n9. **Registration date** (`:176`) \u2014 null \u2192 defaults to today; future \u2192 **400**; then rolled forward to the next business day (skips weekends + fixed 2026 holidays). Sets the adjusted value.\n10. **Per-city cap** \u2014 \u2265 50 owners in that city \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**. (`:185`)\n11. **Per-day cap** \u2014 \u2265 100 owners on that registration date \u2192 **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS**. (`:188`)\n12. **Household assignment** (if postcode present, `:194`) \u2014 computes `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256(`lastName|postcode`), sets it. If household already occupied \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**, unless `sharesHousehold == true` (then flagged as declared member).\n13. **Hard duplicate check** (`:218`) \u2014 `identityKey = telephone|email|householdId`; any match against existing non-deleted owners \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n14. **Soft duplicate flagging** (`:234`) \u2014 declared household member \u2192 `possibleDuplicate=false`; otherwise sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = lowest-id owner sharing last name + postcode but different phone. (Not a rejection.)\n\n## Derived fields set on the entity (before save)\n\n15. `customerCode` \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, de-duplicated against existing codes. (`:240`)\n16. `membershipNumber` \u2014 `<customerCode>-M<fiscalYY>`. (`:242`)\n17. `namesakeCount` \u2014 count of existing owners with same first+last name. (`:243`)\n\n## Persistence\n\n18. **`clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`** (`:244`) \u2014 `@Transactional`, `em.persist` (new id assigned). On flush, Hibernate re-validates entity constraints (`@NotEmpty` on firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone; `@Pattern` on telephone). No `@PrePersist`/`@EntityListeners`; `pets` is empty so no cascade. DB has NOT NULL columns but **no UNIQUE constraints** \u2014 all uniqueness is enforced by the controller logic above.\n\n## After save\n\n19. **Idempotency record** \u2014 if a key was supplied, stores `key \u2192 owner.id`. (`:245`)\n20. **Response mapping** (`toOwnerDto`) computes read-only derived fields (salutation, displayName, initials, timezone, identityKey, checkDigit, etc.). (`:248`)\n21. **Membership scoring** (`applyMembership`, `:249`) \u2014 sets `membershipPoints`/`membershipLevel`.\n22. **Audit logging** \u2014 one `AUDIT.info(\"owner created: ...\")` line. (`:250`)\n23. **Bulk-signup warning** \u2014 sets flag if >80 owners land on today's business day. (`:253`)\n24. **`Location: /api/owners/{id}`** header + **201 CREATED**. (`:254`)\n\n**Notable absences:** no password encoding, no application events, no email/notification sending, no JPA lifecycle callbacks, and no DB-level uniqueness \u2014 confirmed by the trace."
